      "note": "ENH-006 D128 (operator, 2026-11-06): one probe per form, additive; the stack's verdict is that any probe fires. Each probe trains on its own form's disclosures and every non-disclosure row of every form, plus the everyday rows (train only); other forms' disclosures are left out of every split. Render a probe by putting its `owns` in place of {{owns}} and, where `id_test_share` is set, its fractions in place of \"{{split_fractions}}\" (a JSON list, not a string). A probe with no `id_test_share` builds `probe_recipe` on [{{pass2_version}}, {{everyday_version}}]. One with a share builds `resplit_recipe` on [{{pass2_version}}] (its own positives only, redrawn so the in-distribution test holds 20 or more: miStudio refuses a view under 20 of a class), then `probe_recipe` on [{{resplit_version}}, {{stack_negatives_version}}, {{everyday_version}}]; the moved positives' training siblings then cross into id_test, so check and repair (D-4) before binding.",
